D2 is the lever; N is not. At fixed N=64, D2 8->16 moved the ceiling 5.80 -> 8.58; at fixed D2=8,
N 8->64 moved it only 4.65 -> 5.80. Duplicated root work is negligible (+6k nodes on 25.9M = 0.02%).
The depth-1 ceiling is stable at ~1.5x across k, confirming the pool script's "fixed FRACTION" note.

